If the PR has **all approvals** (`reviewDecision == "APPROVED"`) **and**
all CI checks are passing **and** it is not a draft, it is ready to
merge.

**In interactive mode**, offer to merge:

```
mitto_ui_options(self_id: "{{ .Session.ID }}",
  question: "🚀 PR #<number> (<title>) is approved with passing CI. Merge it?",
  options: [
    { label: "Yes, merge now" },
    { label: "No, just notify" }
  ])
```

On "Yes": run `gh pr merge <number>` with the repo scope used elsewhere in
this prompt (e.g. `--repo <owner>/<repo>` or the prompt's `--repo` flag)
and the repo's preferred merge strategy (`--squash`, `--merge`, or
`--rebase` — pick whichever the repo has configured as default). Then
notify success.

**In silent mode** (scheduled loop run), do **not** auto-merge — just
notify:

```
mitto_ui_notify(self_id: "{{ .Session.ID }}",
  title: "🚀 PR #<number> is ready to merge",
  message: "<title> — approved with passing CI, waiting to be merged",
  style: "success")
```
